{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context (operator escalation R3/C11.3, 2026-08-12) — re-scoped 2026-08-11 after a premise audit\n\nThe code-review gate runs its Pass-2 verify judge (gates/code-review.yaml verify step). The\noriginal filing claimed that 0 of ~1,400 recorded code_review_result_v2 sidecar findings carry a\n`verification` block, and asked for the block to be persisted.\n\n**That premise was disproven by a direct audit of the live store and item 1 is withdrawn.** Across\nall 3,669 recorded REVIEW_RESULT events (1,377 code_review_result_v2 + 114 v1), 3,583 of 3,673\npersisted code-review findings (97.5%) already carry `verification`, and every one of those blocks\nholds exactly `{binary, severity_attributes}` — the shape item 1 proposed adding. Presence is\nuniform over time (v1 2026-07: 358/358; v2 2026-07: 1592/1612; v2 2026-08: 1633/1703), so it is\nnot a recent fix. The analysis that produced the \"0 findings\" number read for the plan-review\nfield shape; code-review reaches the same result by a different mechanism —\n`review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings` stamps `verification` onto every decided finding, and\n`code_review.sidecar.build_payload`'s `_with_norm_ids` is a field-SPREAD (`{**f, \"norm_id\": ...}`)\nthat preserves every field, where plan-review's `_slim` is a field-SELECTION that must name\n`verification` explicitly. There is no drop site, and the \"no analog\" claim was incorrect: the\nanalog is preservation rather than selection.\n\nThe 90 findings without a block are all legitimately unverified, not dropped: 53 are `tier=\"DET\"`\n(29 advisory, 24 blocking) plus 8 untiered — deterministic detector / fail-closed / bugfix-size-gate\nfindings that never enter Pass-2, so no verification exists to persist — and 29 are `tier=\"LLM\"`,\n`decision=\"indeterminate\"`, `reason=\"no-verification\"`, where Pass-2 emitted nothing for that index\nand `pass3_decide` degraded them correctly.\n\nWhat survives the audit is the operator's stated larger concern (R3): **nothing errors or warns when\nan expected recording is absent.** `verification_recorded` appears nowhere in `src/`, `tests/`, or\n`docs/`. That gap is real and is the whole of this ticket.\n\nThe original wording of the signal (\"findings lack verification while verify ran\") cannot be\nimplemented as written: it is true on any run carrying a DET-tier detector finding or an\nindeterminate, i.e. routinely, so it would be a standing false alarm. The predicate is therefore\nscoped to the findings that are actually expected to carry a block.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. In `_attach_code_review_metrics` (src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py) — which already computes\n   `verify_requests`, the \"did Pass-2 run\" signal, into `coverage[\"metrics\"]` — add a\n   `verification_recorded` boolean to the same metrics dict.\n2. Detection predicate (LLM-tier-scoped, so it can never become a standing false alarm): over the\n   verdict's `blocking` + `advisory` + `dropped` + `indeterminate` buckets, a finding is EXPECTED to\n   carry a block iff `tier == \"LLM\"` AND `decision != \"indeterminate\"` AND\n   `reason != \"no-verification\"`. DET-tier and untiered findings are excluded (they never enter\n   Pass-2). `verification_recorded` is False iff `verify_requests > 0` AND at least one expected\n   finding has no truthy `verification`; True otherwise.\n3. When the signal is False, log a WARNING naming the missing count out of the expected count, so\n   the absence is both alertable (log) and measurable (metrics key).\n4. Tests: signal cases in tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py (the existing\n   `_attach_code_review_metrics` home) — recorded-true on a healthy verdict, recorded-false with a\n   warning when an expected block is missing, and recorded-true when the ONLY blockless findings are\n   DET-tier / indeterminate (the false-alarm guard). Plus a regression pin in\n   tests/unit/test_code_review_ws4.py asserting the sidecar payload round-trips a finding's\n   `{binary, severity_attributes}` through `build_payload` — pinning today's already-correct\n   behaviour so the field-spread cannot silently regress to a field-selection.\n\nAdvisory only: this touches `coverage[\"metrics\"]` and never `verdict[\"verdict\"]`. Sidecar readers\nare schema-tolerant, so a new metrics key is additive.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `coverage[\"metrics\"][\"verification_recorded\"]` is present on every finalized code-review\n      verdict, and is False with a WARNING naming the missing count when Pass-2 ran but an\n      LLM-tier decided finding carries no verification block. Verify:\n      `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_fp_ledger.py -q`\n- [ ] The signal does NOT fire when the only blockless findings are DET-tier or\n      `decision=\"indeterminate\"` / `reason=\"no-verification\"` — the standing-false-alarm guard.\n      Verify: covered by a dedicated test in the same module.\n- [ ] A sidecar payload round-trips a verified finding's `verification.binary` and\n      `verification.severity_attributes` through `build_payload`. Verify:\n      `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"code_review or sidecar\"`\n- [ ] Existing sidecar readers are unaffected (additive metrics key only). Verify:\n      `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"sidecar\"`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786507843198901001,"uuid":"9356847a-5e98-477f-ac9e-8b937178cfeb"}